P1.8: enforce Mongo auth + harden the mongo/web containers

- docker-compose.yml: mongo now runs with --auth and a root user seeded from
  MONGO_USER/MONGO_PASSWORD; the API's Mongo URI carries those creds
  (authSource=admin). Mongo was reachable unauthenticated by any host-local
  process (API is host-network); loopback binding was the only gate. Now auth is.
- Container hardening: mongo + web get no-new-privileges; web additionally
  cap_drop ALL + cap_add NET_BIND_SERVICE (Caddy 80/443). The api container is
  documented as intentionally privileged (host scanners + sudo + docker.sock) and
  is contained by RBAC + action allow-list + self-protect, not by caps.
- deploy.sh: generate a random URL-safe MONGO_PASSWORD for a fresh .env, and
  backfill one into a pre-auth .env (with a loud warning that an EXISTING mongo
  volume must be recreated for --auth to take effect — the scan catalog
  re-populates, so no real data is lost).
- .env.example: document MONGO_USER/MONGO_PASSWORD and the docker-vs-baremetal split.

MIGRATION (existing deploys): set MONGO_PASSWORD in deploy/docker/.env, then
`docker compose --env-file .env down -v && bash deploy/docker/deploy.sh` to
recreate the Mongo volume with the root user. Rescan to repopulate.

